Disable Machine::check_program bytecode-fingerprint check.

The twin-run design (BLUEPRINT.md) has corrupt parties load mutated
bytecode while honest parties load the original. The fingerprint check
runs in prepare() before any computation, hashes each tape's raw .bc
bytes, broadcasts hashes among parties, and aborts on mismatch. It runs
in every protocol (semi-honest too) — it's a baseline integrity check,
not a malicious-security mechanism. Disabling it lets the harness
exercise the layers that actually matter (MAC checks at OPEN, etc.).

See notes/mpspdz-patching.md for the broader plan.

